secrets/

# User directory mounts (generated by pai onboard)
docker-compose.override.yml
.user-dirs.json

# PKI certificates and private keys (generated by pai onboard).
# Anchored to repo root ONLY — an unanchored pki/ also ignored the SOURCE
# module src/pai_metis/pki/, which is how that code got lost once.
/pki/

# Rust build artifacts
target/

# large local model weights (17GB) - never commit
models/
# ...but two tracked directories are not weights: a doc and a UI mock fixture.
# A pattern this broad silently dropped them from the first public snapshot
# (a fresh `git add -A` ignores a tracked path); tests/test_tracked_files_are_not_ignored.py
# now fails when any tracked file matches an ignore rule.
!docs/models/
!ui/mock/fixtures/GET/api/models/
# build-cross.sh artifacts. This listed ONLY -arm64, so an amd64 build (what
# the controller produces for a GPU worker) was untracked-but-not-ignored and
# a `git add -A` would have committed a 9 MB binary. Cover every GOOS/GOARCH
# for both binaries instead of enumerating the ones seen so far.
node-agent-go/pai-node-agent-*
node-agent-go/pai-hostd-*
# === bloat & secrets hardening (2026-06-21) ===
# secrets / keys
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.keystore
# ONE narrow exception: the gateway's birth-proof TEST fixtures.
# `gateway-rust/src/birth_proof.rs` include_str!()s them, so an ignored fixture
# is not a skipped test — it is a COMPILE failure in CI against a file that
# exists only on the author's machine. This throwaway RSA-2048 material is
# generated for the test suite and protects nothing; a real birth key is
# generated per node at enrollment and never leaves it. The `.test{key,cert}.`
# infix keeps the exception from ever widening to a real key.
!gateway-rust/src/fixtures/*.testkey.pem
!gateway-rust/src/fixtures/*.testcert.pem
secrets/
.env.local
.env.bak*
.env.*.bak
# model weights & large binaries
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pt
# Local model-conversion scratch (HF download -> Modelfile -> gguf). The
# weights were already covered above, but a HuggingFace checkout is mostly
# NOT weights: the tokenizer/vocab/merges files are plain JSON and text, so
# they sailed past every pattern here. One 0.6B model staged 909,814 lines
# (tokenizer.json alone is 757k) against a repo whose entire tracked history
# is smaller. This is a working directory, not a source artifact.
.model-convert/
*.pth
*.onnx
